{
  "title": "Filter standalone yield sentences from ingredient lines",
  "description": "While rerunning `make pipeline` for \
`p4-audit-non-ingredient-parenthetical-notes`, the generated ingredient \
parsing fixture for \
`cocktailswithsuderman.substack.com/p/lol-its-an-appletini` exposed a \
standalone yield sentence being parsed as an ingredient:\n\
\n\
  - Raw: `(This makes a 12-ounce batch.)`\n\
  - Current item: `This makes a 12-ounce batch.`\n\
\n\
This is recipe metadata rather than an ingredient. Audit whether similar \
standalone parenthetical yield/count sentences appear elsewhere, then filter \
or route them outside ingredient parsing without losing real ingredient notes \
like `(about 10 raspberries)`.",
